# The repository stores CRLF line endings -- `dpu/src/pool.zig` has 292 CR bytes
# in its blob, not 0 -- and `zig fmt --check` is one of the gate's steps.
#
# Without this file, a default Windows clone has `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# re-smudges those already-CRLF blobs into CRCRLF. Measured: `pool.zig` goes
# from 292 CR bytes to 473, `build.zig` from 863 to 1281, and `zig fmt --check`
# then fails on all eleven Zig files, so `zig build check` is red out of the box
# on the platform this project is developed on.
#
# Worse, `git status` still reports the tree as clean while it is corrupted, so
# nothing surfaces the problem until the gate runs.
#
# Marking everything non-text makes the checkout byte-exact whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says, and git still renders text diffs for these files rather
# than calling them binary.
* -text
